//@version=6
indicator("Lucky: MTF Trend & Breakout Dashboard", shorttitle="Lucky MTF", overlay=true, max_bars_back=1000, max_lines_count=150, max_labels_count=150, max_boxes_count=50)

//====================================================================
// Section #1 | INDICATOR GUIDE & STRATEGY
//====================================================================
//
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  ALL VITAL TREND AND BREAKOUT INDICATOR
//  with Multi-Timeframe Bias Table
//  Pine Script v6  |  TradingView Overlay Indicator
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//
// ── WHAT IS THIS INDICATOR? ─────────────────────────────────────────
//  This is an all-in-one trend-following and breakout confluence
//  indicator. It combines nine proven technical tools into a single
//  overlay: Moving Averages, VWAP, MACD, ZLSMA, UT Bot (adaptive
//  trailing stop), Supertrend, ADX, RSI, and an Opening Range
//  Breakout (ORB) system. A Multi-Timeframe Bias Table summarises
//  the state of all these tools across up to eight timeframes
//  simultaneously, giving you an instant "dashboard" view of market
//  direction. A live Price Point Dashboard (PPD) shows key daily
//  levels: MAs, pivot points, 52-week high, Fibonacci levels, and
//  VWAP — all updated in real time.
//
// ── HOW TO USE THIS INDICATOR ───────────────────────────────────────
//  STEP 1 – Set your Moving Averages (Section #3 → MA group).
//           Default: Fast EMA 10, Medium EMA 20, Long SMA 200.
//           Keep Fast < Medium < Long at all times.
//
//  STEP 2 – Enable the Bias Table (Settings → MARKET BIAS TABLE).
//           Select which timeframes to display (1m, 5m, 15m, 30m,
//           1h, 2h, 4h, Daily). Each row shows a Y/N signal and
//           an average agreement % across all active timeframes.
//           Aim for ≥70% agreement before entering a trade.
//
//  STEP 3 – Wait for a UT Bot Buy or Sell label to appear on the
//           chart. This is your primary entry trigger. The label
//           fires when the adaptive trailing stop flips direction
//           with volume confirmation.
//
//  STEP 4 – Confirm with Supertrend direction and MACD > Signal.
//           Ideally both agree with the UT Bot signal direction.
//
//  STEP 5 – Use the auto-plotted Stop Loss line for risk management.
//           Take Profit lines at R1, R1.5, R2, and R3 are plotted
//           automatically from the entry price.
//
//  STEP 6 – Check the Price Point Dashboard (bottom-right) for
//           key daily support/resistance before placing your trade.
//
//  STEP 7 – Check the Trade Probability Score in the dashboard.
//           A score of 60 or above indicates a Good Setup. 80 or
//           above is a High Probability setup. Below 40 is Avoid.
//           Use this as a final confluence gate before entering.
//
// ── BEST TIMEFRAMES ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  • Day Trading:      5-minute or 15-minute charts
//  • Swing Trading:    1-hour or 4-hour charts
//  • Position Trading: Daily chart
//  The Bias Table always shows higher timeframe context regardless
//  of which chart timeframe you are currently viewing.
//
// ── BEST TRADING STYLE / STRATEGY ──────────────────────────────────
//  This indicator is optimised for TREND-FOLLOWING with BREAKOUT
//  confirmation. It works best when:
//  • The market is trending (avoid ranging/choppy markets).
//  • VIX is below 22 (BULLISH reading in the Bias Table).
//  • The ORB row shows ABOVE 15, ABOVE 30, or ABOVE 60 (bullish
//    breakout above the opening range).
//  • At least 6 of 8 bias rows show "Y" for your direction.
//  • You enter on UT Bot labels and exit at TP2 (2R) or TP3 (3R).
//
//  Recommended entry checklist:
//   [1] Bias Table ≥70% agreement in your direction
//   [2] UT Bot Buy/Sell label confirmed on bar close
//   [3] Supertrend agrees (bullish = price above green line)
//   [4] MACD > Signal (for longs) / MACD < Signal (for shorts)
//   [5] Price above/below VWAP (use PPD dashboard VWAP row)
//   [6] VIX = BULLISH or NEUTRAL (not BEARISH for longs)
//   [7] ADX ≥ 20 (trend is strong enough to trade)
//   [8] Trade Probability Score ≥ 60 (Good Setup or higher)
//
// ── VITAL TIPS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//  • Enable "Draw visuals only on bar close" to eliminate repainting.
//  • Use the Swing Filter (enabled by default) to avoid signals
//    during sideways price action.
//  • The 3 Day, Weekly, Monthly, and Quarterly Bias rows are hidden
//    on futures symbols and on charts with < 5000 bars of history,
//    because the slope calculation needs sufficient historical data.
//  • "Freeze TP when touched" preserves your TP lines even after
//    price retraces, so you can see which targets were hit.
//  • On Daily/Weekly/Monthly charts the Bias Table automatically
//    switches to show D / W / M columns instead of intraday TFs.
//  • All request.security() calls are consolidated to 22 total
//    (well under TradingView's 40-call limit) for fast loading.
//
// ── CANDLESTICK PATTERN GUIDE ────────────────────────────────────────
//
//  IMPORTANT — TIMEFRAME: All candlestick patterns are detected on
//  the EXACT SAME timeframe as your chart. On a 15m chart, every
//  pattern uses 15m candle data. There is no separate timeframe
//  calculation. Labels appear on the bar where the pattern completed.
//
//  LABEL NAMES ON THE CHART:
//  "BullEngulf"  = Bullish Engulfing
//  "BearEngulf"  = Bearish Engulfing
//  "Hammer"      = Hammer
//  "ShootStar"   = Shooting Star
//  "MornStar"    = Morning Star
//  "EveStar"     = Evening Star
//  "InsideBar"   = Inside Bar
//  "TweezTop"    = Tweezer Top
//  "TweezBot"    = Tweezer Bottom
//  "Doji"        = Standard Doji
//  "Dragonfly"   = Dragonfly Doji
//  "Gravestone"  = Gravestone Doji
//  "SweepHigh"   = Liquidity Sweep of a Recent High (bearish rejection)
//  "SweepLow"    = Liquidity Sweep of a Recent Low  (bullish rejection
//
//  BULLISH ENGULFING  →  label: "BullEngulf"  🟢
//  A large green candle whose body completely covers ("engulfs") the
//  entire body of the prior red candle. The current candle must open
//  BELOW the prior close and close ABOVE the prior open. Signals a
//  sharp shift from selling to buying pressure. Most reliable at a
//  support level or after a pullback with above-average volume.
//
//  BEARISH ENGULFING  →  label: "BearEngulf"  🔴
//  A large red candle whose body completely engulfs the prior green
//  candle's body. Current open ABOVE prior close, current close BELOW
//  prior open. Signals sellers have seized control. Most powerful at
//  resistance levels or after a rally with above-average volume.
//
//  HAMMER  →  label: "Hammer"  🔨
//  A single-candle bullish reversal with a very specific shape:
//  lower wick ≥ 2× the body length, upper wick ≤ 30% of total range.
//  The small body sits at the TOP of the candle with the long tail
//  pointing DOWN. Only fires when: price is near a 20-bar low (within
//  0.5%), the prior candle was red (downtrend context), RSI is below
//  50 and rising, and volume is above the 5-bar average.
//
//  SHOOTING STAR  →  label: "ShootStar"  ⭐
//  Mirror image of the Hammer. Upper wick ≥ 2× body, lower wick ≤ 30%
//  of total range. Small body at the BOTTOM of the candle, long spike
//  pointing UP. Only fires when: price is near a 20-bar high (within
//  1%), prior candle was green (uptrend context), RSI is above 50 and
//  falling, volume is normal or below average (exhaustion signal).
//
//  MORNING STAR  →  label: "MornStar"  🌅
//  A 3-candle bullish reversal pattern at the bottom of a downtrend:
//  (1) A large red candle continuing the downtrend.
//  (2) A small-bodied candle with low volume (indecision — the "star").
//  (3) A large green candle closing ABOVE bar 1's high on high volume.
//  RSI must be below 35 two bars prior (oversold). MACD crossover or
//  price above the medium MA on bar 3 confirms the reversal.
//
//  EVENING STAR  →  label: "EveStar"  🌆
//  The bearish counterpart to Morning Star. 3-candle top reversal:
//  (1) A large green candle extending the uptrend.
//  (2) A small-bodied star candle at the top on low volume.
//  (3) A large red candle closing BELOW bar 1's low on high volume.
//  RSI must be above 65 two bars prior (overbought).
//
//  INSIDE BAR  →  label: "InsideBar"  📦
//  A candle whose entire range (high to low) fits within the prior
//  candle's range. Signals consolidation or a pause in trend. Strict
//  mode (default) requires the prior (mother) bar to be at least 0.8×
//  ATR so tiny inside bars on sleepy candles are suppressed. Most
//  useful when it forms at a key level or following a strong trend bar.
//  On 15m charts for high-beta stocks, watch for breakout of the
//  mother bar range as an entry trigger.
//
//  TWEEZER TOP  →  label: "TweezTop"  🔩
//  Two consecutive candles with nearly identical highs, indicating
//  that buyers tried twice to push price higher but were rejected at
//  the same level. The ATR-based tolerance prevents requiring pixel-
//  perfect matching. Context filter requires a prior upward move
//  (close[1] > close[3]) to make the rejection meaningful. Best used
//  at known resistance zones or after a sustained rally.
//
//  TWEEZER BOTTOM  →  label: "TweezBot"  🔩
//  Mirror image of the Tweezer Top. Two candles with nearly identical
//  lows showing repeated buyer support at the same price. Context
//  filter requires a prior downward move (close[1] < close[3]).
//  Most powerful at known support zones or after a sustained decline.
//
//  DOJI  →  label: "Doji" / "Dragonfly" / "Gravestone"  ✝
//  A candle with an extremely small real body relative to its total
//  range (configurable max body % of range, default 5%). Signals
//  indecision between buyers and sellers.
//  • Standard Doji: wicks on both sides, tiny body.
//  • Dragonfly Doji: lower wick ≥ 60% of range, almost no upper wick.
//    Bullish implication — strong lower tail showing buyers defended.
//  • Gravestone Doji: upper wick ≥ 60% of range, almost no lower wick.
//    Bearish implication — long upper spike showing sellers rejected
//    the advance. Equivalent to a Shooting Star with a doji body.
//
//  HOW TO USE PATTERNS WITH THIS INDICATOR:
//  • Use patterns as CONFIRMATION, not as standalone entry signals.
//  • A BullEngulf or Hammer that fires while the Bias Table shows
//    ≥70% bullish agreement is a high-conviction long setup.
//  • A BearEngulf or ShootStar at a PPD resistance level (Pivot R1,
//    52 Wk High, Fibonacci level) is a strong short signal.
//  • MornStar / EveStar on the 15m or 1h chart are the rarest but
//    most reliable patterns — always note when they appear alongside
//    a UT Bot label in the same direction.
//  • InsideBar breakouts are high-probability on 15m charts when the
//    mother bar was a strong trend bar (high volume, wide range).
//  • TweezTop/Bottom gains significance when it appears at the PPD
//    Pivot R1/S1 or Previous Day High/Low levels.
//
// ── PHASE 2 FEATURES ────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
//  Five new analytical tools have been added to the Price Point
//  Dashboard. All are visible in the bottom-right dashboard and
//  can be toggled individually under their respective settings
//  groups (PHASE 2 ▶ ...).
//
//  TREND STRENGTH SCORE (TSS) — 0 to 100
//  A composite score measuring how strongly the current bar is
//  aligned with a bullish trend. Five weighted components:
//   • EMA Alignment       25 pts  fast > medium > long MA
//   • VWAP Location       20 pts  price above session VWAP
//   • MACD Alignment      20 pts  MACD line above Signal line
//   • Supertrend Dir      20 pts  Supertrend in bullish state
//   • ADX Strength        15 pts  tiered: ≥40=15, ≥30=12, ≥20=8
//  Reading guide: 70–100 = strong trend, 50–69 = moderate,
//  30–49 = weak, 0–29 = no trend or bearish.
//
//  TRADE PROBABILITY SCORE (TPS) — 0 to 100
//  A 12-factor setup quality score for long entries. Each factor
//  contributes a weighted portion of the total 100 points:
//   • MTF Alignment       20 pts  average bullish % across active TFs
//   • EMA Stack           10 pts  fast > medium > long MA
//   • VWAP Location        8 pts  price above VWAP
//   • Price > MA200         7 pts  price above 200-period MA
//   • MACD Alignment        8 pts  MACD line above Signal line
//   • Supertrend Dir       10 pts  bullish direction
//   • ADX Strength          8 pts  tiered ADX reading
//   • Relative Volume       7 pts  elevated vs average volume
//   • ORB Status            7 pts  above 15/30/60-min opening range
//   • RS vs Benchmark 1     5 pts  outperforming QQQ (or custom)
//   • Volatility State      5 pts  Normal or Expansion preferred
//   • Key Level Proximity   5 pts  above Pivot S1, below Pivot R1
//  Interpretation: 80–100 = High Probability, 60–79 = Good Setup,
//  40–59 = Neutral, 0–39 = Avoid.
//
//  LIQUIDITY SWEEP DETECTION
//  Detects when price wicks through a recent swing level then
//  closes back inside it — a classic stop-hunt pattern.
//   • "SweepHigh" label (red, above bar): price exceeded a recent
//     swing high but closed below it. Bearish rejection signal.
//     Sellers absorbed breakout buyers above the prior high.
//   • "SweepLow" label (teal, below bar): price dipped under a
//     recent swing low but closed above it. Bullish reversal signal.
//     Buyers absorbed stop-hunt sellers below the prior low.
//  Use "Lookback Bars" to set how many prior bars define the swing
//  reference level. Use "Min Wick (× ATR)" to filter out small
//  wicks — higher values produce fewer but more selective signals.
//  Enable "Bar Close Only" to prevent real-time repainting.
//
//  RELATIVE STRENGTH vs BENCHMARKS
//  Compares this symbol's intraday return (from prior day close)
//  against two configurable benchmarks, defaulting to QQQ and SPY.
//  Formula: RS = Symbol Return % − Benchmark Return %
//  Positive = outperforming the benchmark today.
//  Negative = underperforming the benchmark today.
//  Use this to confirm institutional interest: strong setups
//  typically show positive RS vs both QQQ and SPY simultaneously.
//  Benchmarks can be changed to any TradingView symbol in
//  Settings → PHASE 2 ▶ RELATIVE STRENGTH.
//
//  VOLATILITY STATE  —  SQUEEZE / NORMAL / EXPANSION
//  Uses Bollinger Band width relative to Keltner Channel width
//  to classify the current volatility environment (TTM Squeeze
//  style detection):
//   • SQUEEZE    = BB bands are inside the Keltner Channel.
//                  Volatility has compressed. A directional move
//                  is likely approaching. Wait for confirmation.
//   • NORMAL     = Standard volatility environment.
//                  Trend-following signals are most reliable here.
//   • EXPANSION  = BB width exceeds 1.5× its 20-bar average.
//                  Volatility is expanding. Momentum entries have
//                  an edge but risk is elevated. Widen stops.
//
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ── PHASE 2 FEATURES ────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
//  Five new analytical tools have been added to the Price Point
//  Dashboard. All are visible in the bottom-right dashboard and
//  can be toggled individually under their respective settings
//  groups (PHASE 2 ▶ ...).
//
//  TREND STRENGTH SCORE (TSS) — 0 to 100
//  A composite score measuring how strongly the current bar is
//  aligned with a bullish trend. Five weighted components:
//   • EMA Alignment       25 pts  fast > medium > long MA
//   • VWAP Location       20 pts  price above session VWAP
//   • MACD Alignment      20 pts  MACD line above Signal line
//   • Supertrend Dir      20 pts  Supertrend in bullish state
//   • ADX Strength        15 pts  tiered: ≥40=15, ≥30=12, ≥20=8
//  Reading guide: 70–100 = strong trend, 50–69 = moderate,
//  30–49 = weak, 0–29 = no trend or bearish.
//
//  TRADE PROBABILITY SCORE (TPS) — 0 to 100
//  A 12-factor setup quality score for long entries. Each factor
//  contributes a weighted portion of the total 100 points:
//   • MTF Alignment       20 pts  average bullish % across active TFs
//   • EMA Stack           10 pts  fast > medium > long MA
//   • VWAP Location        8 pts  price above VWAP
//   • Price > MA200         7 pts  price above 200-period MA
//   • MACD Alignment        8 pts  MACD line above Signal line
//   • Supertrend Dir       10 pts  bullish direction
//   • ADX Strength          8 pts  tiered ADX reading
//   • Relative Volume       7 pts  elevated vs average volume
//   • ORB Status            7 pts  above 15/30/60-min opening range
//   • RS vs Benchmark 1     5 pts  outperforming QQQ (or custom)
//   • Volatility State      5 pts  Normal or Expansion preferred
//   • Key Level Proximity   5 pts  above Pivot S1, below Pivot R1
//  Interpretation: 80–100 = High Probability, 60–79 = Good Setup,
//  40–59 = Neutral, 0–39 = Avoid.
//
//  LIQUIDITY SWEEP DETECTION
//  Detects when price wicks through a recent swing level then
//  closes back inside it — a classic stop-hunt pattern.
//   • "SweepHigh" label (red, above bar): price exceeded a recent
//     swing high but closed below it. Bearish rejection signal.
//     Sellers absorbed breakout buyers above the prior high.
//   • "SweepLow" label (teal, below bar): price dipped under a
//     recent swing low but closed above it. Bullish reversal signal.
//     Buyers absorbed stop-hunt sellers below the prior low.
//  Use "Lookback Bars" to set how many prior bars define the swing
//  reference level. Use "Min Wick (× ATR)" to filter out small
//  wicks — higher values produce fewer but more selective signals.
//  Enable "Bar Close Only" to prevent real-time repainting.
//
//  RELATIVE STRENGTH vs BENCHMARKS
//  Compares this symbol's intraday return (from prior day close)
//  against two configurable benchmarks, defaulting to QQQ and SPY.
//  Formula: RS = Symbol Return % − Benchmark Return %
//  Positive = outperforming the benchmark today.
//  Negative = underperforming the benchmark today.
//  Use this to confirm institutional interest: strong setups
//  typically show positive RS vs both QQQ and SPY simultaneously.
//  Benchmarks can be changed to any TradingView symbol in
//  Settings → PHASE 2 ▶ RELATIVE STRENGTH.
//
//  VOLATILITY STATE  —  SQUEEZE / NORMAL / EXPANSION
//  Uses Bollinger Band width relative to Keltner Channel width
//  to classify the current volatility environment (TTM Squeeze
//  style detection):
//   • SQUEEZE    = BB bands are inside the Keltner Channel.
//                  Volatility has compressed. A directional move
//                  is likely approaching. Wait for confirmation.
//   • NORMAL     = Standard volatility environment.
//                  Trend-following signals are most reliable here.
//   • EXPANSION  = BB width exceeds 1.5× its 20-bar average.
//                  Volatility is expanding. Momentum entries have
//                  an edge but risk is elevated. Widen stops.
//
// ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//====================================================================
// Section #2 | GROUPS
//====================================================================
GROUP_MA     = "================== MOVING AVERAGE ==================="
GROUP_VWAP   = "==================== VWAP SETTINGS =================="
GROUP_MACD   = "======================== MACD ======================="
GROUP_ZLSMA  = "=============== ZLSMA - ZERO LAG SMA ================"
GROUP_UT     = "================== UT BOT SETTINGS =================="
GROUP_SL     = "STOP LOSS __________________________________________"
GROUP_TP     = "TAKE PROFIT _________________________________________"
GROUP_ST     = "===================== SUPERTREND ===================="
GROUP_ALERTS = "============== LONG / SHORT SIGNALS ================="
GROUP_ADX    = "ADX _________________________________________________"
GROUP_RSI    = "RSI _________________________________________________"
GROUP_LBL    = "==================== EXTRA LABELS ==================="
GROUP_CNDL   = "CANDLESTICKS ________________________________________"
GROUP_BIAS   = "================ MARKET BIAS TABLE =================="
GROUP_TF     = "TIME FRAMES _________________________________________"
GROUP_ORB    = "ORB INDICATOR _______________________________________"
GROUP_PPD    = "========== PRICE POINT LIVE DASHBOARD ==============="
GROUP_SWEEP  = "PHASE 2 ▶ LIQUIDITY SWEEPS _______________________"
GROUP_RS     = "PHASE 2 ▶ RELATIVE STRENGTH ______________________"
GROUP_VOL2   = "PHASE 2 ▶ VOLATILITY STATE _______________________"
GROUP_TPS    = "PHASE 2 ▶ TREND & TRADE SCORES __________________"

//====================================================================
// Section #3 | INPUTS
//====================================================================
const string maInfo = "MA Types: EMA, SMA, WMA, VWMA, RMA, HMA.\nKeep Fast < Medium < Medium-Long < Long."

showMAPlots   = input.bool(true,  "Show all MA Lines",    group=GROUP_MA)
showFastMA    = input.bool(true,  "Fast MA",              group=GROUP_MA, inline="rowF")
maShortLen    = input.int(10,     "Length",               group=GROUP_MA, inline="rowF", minval=1)
maFastType    = input.string("EMA","Type", options=["EMA","SMA","WMA","VWMA","RMA","HMA"], group=GROUP_MA, inline="rowF", tooltip=maInfo)

showMedMA     = input.bool(true,  "Medium MA",            group=GROUP_MA, inline="rowM")
maMedLen      = input.int(20,     "Length",               group=GROUP_MA, inline="rowM", minval=1)
maMedType     = input.string("EMA","Type", options=["EMA","SMA","WMA","VWMA","RMA","HMA"], group=GROUP_MA, inline="rowM", tooltip=maInfo)

showMidLongMA = input.bool(false, "Medium-Long MA",       group=GROUP_MA, inline="rowI")
maMidLongLen  = input.int(50,     "Length",               group=GROUP_MA, inline="rowI", minval=1)
maMidLongType = input.string("SMA","Type", options=["EMA","SMA","WMA","VWMA","RMA","HMA"], group=GROUP_MA, inline="rowI", tooltip=maInfo)

showLongMA    = input.bool(true,  "Long MA",              group=GROUP_MA, inline="rowL")
ma200Len      = input.int(200,    "Length",               group=GROUP_MA, inline="rowL", minval=1)
maLongType    = input.string("SMA","Type", options=["EMA","SMA","WMA","VWMA","RMA","HMA"], group=GROUP_MA, inline="rowL", tooltip=maInfo)

showVWAP      = input.bool(false, "Show VWAP",                    group=GROUP_VWAP, inline="vwA")
hideonDWM     = input.bool(true,  "Hide VWAP on 1D or above",     group=GROUP_VWAP, inline="vwA")
anchor        = input.string("Session", "Anchor Period", options=["Session","Day","Week","Month","Quarter","Year"], group=GROUP_VWAP)
srcVWAP       = input.source(hlc3, "Source",                      group=GROUP_VWAP, inline="vwS")
offsetBars    = input.int(0,      "Offset",                       group=GROUP_VWAP, inline="vwS", minval=0)
calcModeInput = input.string("Standard Deviation", "Bands Calculation Mode", options=["Standard Deviation","Percentage"], group=GROUP_VWAP)
bands1On      = input.bool(true,  "Show Bands", group=GROUP_VWAP, inline="vwB")
bandMult1     = input.float(1.0,  "X1",         group=GROUP_VWAP, inline="vwB", step=0.5, minval=0.0)
bands2On      = input.bool(false, "Show Bands", group=GROUP_VWAP, inline="vwC")
bandMult2     = input.float(2.0,  "X2",         group=GROUP_VWAP, inline="vwC", step=0.5, minval=0.0)
bands3On      = input.bool(false, "Show Bands", group=GROUP_VWAP, inline="vwD")
bandMult3     = input.float(3.0,  "X3",         group=GROUP_VWAP, inline="vwD", step=0.5, minval=0.0)

macdSrc       = input.source(close, "MACD Source",              group=GROUP_MACD)
macdFast      = input.int(12,  "MACD Fast",    group=GROUP_MACD, inline="macd1", minval=1)
macdSlow      = input.int(26,  "MACD Slow",    group=GROUP_MACD, inline="macd1", minval=1)
macdSig       = input.int(9,   "MACD Signal",  group=GROUP_MACD, inline="macd1", minval=1)
distanceThrPct = input.float(0.2, "Min MA Distance %",          group=GROUP_MACD, minval=0.0)
atrLen        = input.int(14,  "ATR Length",                    group=GROUP_MACD, minval=1)
macdSepFactor = input.float(0.1,  "MACD Min Separation (xATR)", group=GROUP_MACD, minval=0.0)

showZLSMA     = input.bool(false, "Show ZLSMA",  group=GROUP_ZLSMA, inline="zlsA")
zlsmaSrc      = input.source(close, "Source",    group=GROUP_ZLSMA, inline="zlsA")
zlsmaLength   = input.int(75,  "Length",         group=GROUP_ZLSMA, inline="zls", minval=2)
zlsmaOffset   = input.int(0,   "Offset",         group=GROUP_ZLSMA, inline="zls")

utShowLine    = input.bool(false, "Show UT Bot Line",             group=GROUP_UT, inline="utA")
utShowLabels  = input.bool(true,  "Show Buy/Sell Labels",         group=GROUP_UT, inline="utA")
entryShow     = input.bool(false, "Show Entry Label",             group=GROUP_UT, inline="utB")
drawUtvizOnClose = input.bool(true,"Draw visuals only on bar close", group=GROUP_UT, inline="utC")
utKey         = input.float(1.2,  "Sensitivity", group=GROUP_UT,  inline="utAT", minval=0.1, step=0.1)
utAtrPeriod   = input.int(7,      "Period",       group=GROUP_UT,  inline="utAT", minval=1)
utColorBars   = input.bool(false, "Color bars by UT trend",       group=GROUP_UT)

utUsePctFilter   = input.bool(false, "Use % Change Filter",       group=GROUP_UT, inline="utF")
utPctThr         = input.float(0.05, "Min % Change",              group=GROUP_UT, inline="utF", minval=0.0, step=0.05)
utUseSwingFilter = input.bool(true,  "Use Swing Filter",          group=GROUP_UT, inline="utS")
